# SalesView — Cursor Project Rules

## Project overview

SalesView is a **single-page, frontend-only React + Vite dashboard** for a
sales team. It loads mocked data from local JSON files and renders monthly
KPIs, a vendor breakdown table and a category breakdown panel.

There is **no backend, no database, no authentication, no external API**.

## Stack

- React 18 + Vite (vanilla JS / JSX, no TypeScript).
- Plain CSS (no CSS-in-JS, no Tailwind, no UI framework).
- No charting library (Chart.js, Recharts, D3, etc.). All visual bars are
  built with plain `<div>`s and `width: {pct}%`.

## File / component conventions

- One component per file under `src/components/`, named in PascalCase
  (`KPICards.jsx`, `SalesTable.jsx`, `CategoryBreakdown.jsx`,
  `PeriodFilter.jsx`, `Header.jsx`).
- Pure helpers go under `src/utils/` (`format.js`, `periods.js`,
  `calculations.js`). Components should not duplicate calculation logic.
- App composition lives in `src/App.jsx`. State (active period, derived
  ranges, etc.) is owned there and passed down via props.
- Styles live in a single `src/styles.css` keyed off `sv-*` class names and
  CSS variables defined in `:root`.

## Data

- All data is mocked and lives under `data/`:
  - `data/sales.json` — list of transactions
    (`{ id, vendedor, categoria, monto, fecha }`).
  - `data/team.json` — vendor roster (`{ nombre, color }`).
  - `data/config.json` — `meta_mensual`, `nombre_equipo`, `fecha_referencia`.
- Data is imported directly with `import x from '../data/x.json'`. Vite
  handles JSON imports natively.
- The dashboard uses `config.fecha_referencia` as "today" so the demo is
  deterministic — do not call `new Date()` for the reference date.
- All date math is done in **UTC** with helpers in `src/utils/periods.js`.
- To regenerate mock data, run `npm run generate-data`. The generator in
  `scripts/generate-data.mjs` is seeded for reproducibility.

## Design system

Defined as CSS custom properties in `src/styles.css`:

| Token             | Value      | Use                                  |
| ----------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------ |
| `--color-bg`      | `#F1F5F9`  | App background                       |
| `--color-surface` | `#FFFFFF`  | Card background                      |
| `--color-primary` | `#1E3A5F`  | Header, KPI left-border, accents     |
| `--color-pos`     | `#10B981`  | Positive deltas (↑)                  |
| `--color-neg`     | `#EF4444`  | Negative deltas (↓)                  |
| `--color-text`    | `#0F172A`  | Primary text                         |
| `--color-text-muted` | `#64748B` | Secondary text                    |
| `--color-border`  | `#E2E8F0`  | Dividers / borders                   |

Category colors (used in `CategoryBreakdown.jsx`):

- Electrónica `#3B82F6`
- Ropa `#8B5CF6`
- Hogar `#F59E0B`
- Alimentos `#10B981`
- Deportes `#EF4444`

Typography:

- `Inter` (Google Fonts) with `system-ui` fallback.
- KPI numbers: 28–32px / weight 700.
- Delta percentages: 14px / weight 600.
- Table column headers: 13px / weight 600 / uppercase with tracking.
- Table data: 14px / weight 400. Money columns: weight 600.

Visual conventions:

- KPI cards use `--shadow-card`, a 4px left border in `--color-primary`,
  and an emoji icon on the left.
- Meta progress bar uses a gradient from `--color-primary` to `#3B82F6`.
- Category bars and vendor share bars use the entity color and rounded
  ends (`--radius-pill`).
- Hover states only shift background to `--color-surface-alt`.
- Transitions: 200ms `ease` for color/background/width changes.

## Hard constraints (what NOT to add)

- ❌ No login / auth.
- ❌ No charting libraries. Bars are plain CSS only.
- ❌ No PDF / Excel export.
- ❌ No dark mode. Light mode only.
- ❌ No real-time data, no fetch / no external APIs.
- ❌ No data editing UI. The dashboard is read-only.
- ❌ No complex animations. Only short CSS transitions.
- ❌ No routing / no multi-page setup. One page only.
- ❌ No tooltips or popovers.
- ❌ No notifications, no toasts.
- ❌ No footer.

## When extending the codebase

- Prefer adding logic to `src/utils/*` and keeping components presentational.
- Reuse the existing CSS variables instead of hard-coding colors.
- Keep numeric formatting in `src/utils/format.js` (`formatMoney`,
  `formatPercentChange`, etc.) — do not call `toLocaleString` directly in
  components.
- All new period options must go through `getPeriodRange` in
  `src/utils/periods.js` so KPI / table / category breakdowns recompute
  consistently.
